{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to","id":1209701,"title":"Beasts interactions with Lair HOW-TO","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-21T11:22:47-07:00","id":1209701,"title":"Beasts interactions with Lair HOW-TO","content":"So I got some doubts how being Begotten works, even after reading<b> Beast Player's Guide</b>. Beast is human host of Primordial Dream Horror that is in the Lair Chamber(s) in Dream. <b>BPG</b> points that Beast and Horror becomes truly One when Beasts enters the Lair and merging, with Beast 'at wheel' of this nightmarish monster being.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure I get it right on what happens to human body of Beast - Is it still in the material world, laying comatose when Beast now riding it's own Horror in Dream? Or material body of Beasts simply vanish when she cross the Pathways and for the time being - until she leaves her Lair - she IS her Horror, and her material body is no more in existence? So how this works? I suspect second option, but descriptions are not direct on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-22-2018, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T11:33:02-07:00","id":1209705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to#post1209701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I got some doubts how being Begotten works, even after reading<b> Beast Player's Guide</b>. Beast is human host of Primordial Dream Horror that is in the Lair Chamber(s) in Dream. <b>BPG</b> points that Beast and Horror becomes truly One when Beasts enters the Lair and merging, with Beast 'at wheel' of this nightmarish monster being.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure I get it right on what happens to human body of Beast - is it still in the material world, laying comatose when Beast now riding it's own Horror in Dream? Or material body of Beasts simply vanish when she cross the Pathways and for the time being - until she leaves her Lair - she IS her Horror, and her material body is no more in existence? So how this works? I suspect second option, but descriptions are not direct on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the second option - the Beast's body physically merges into the Horror/Beast fusion-creature.<br /> <br /> Also, you could stand to ask all these questions in the Beast questions thread as opposed to starting a new thread for each one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T11:44:27-07:00","id":1209710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1209705#post1209705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the second option - the Beast's body physically merges into the Horror/Beast fusion-creature.<br /> <br /> Also, you could stand to ask all these questions in the Beast questions thread as opposed to starting a new thread for each one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed on both points. The very point of the Ask a Simple Question threads is to prevent this sort of clutter that makes it harder to find specific threads and maybe even taxes the site's memory limits (I dunno how the code works)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:37:10-07:00","id":1209735,"title":"","content":"I created topic as I just getting started here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So the human host body vanishes on entering the Lair, on the merging with Horror.<br /> <br /> But then question is - <b>HOW Beast opens way to the Lair?</b> Is it classical portal, like large circle in one way of physical side of location, showing interior of the Lair inside it? Or does only Beast summons Traits of Lair and vanishes, changing the real location for the Primordial one, melting in the thin air? If it is portal - someone can easily follow here through. If it is vanishing - it's impossible to come on her. On first scenario I can easily see Heroes going after Beast by her Lair on portal still working. On second take it will be difficult even for broodmates to join Beast, as there is literally nothing more for them to follow her through. So what's is game answer and it's implication?<br /> <br /> Edit: It seems it's take three - physical location and Dream Chamber overlaps for number of turn. Thanks, <b>Wormwood</b>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-22-2018, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:43:46-07:00","id":1209738,"title":"","content":"I concur with both Master and ajf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> When a Beast opens a Primordial Pathway, the current physical location and the Chamber's Primordial counterpart overlap - the Primordial Chamber becomes the current physical location for a certain amount of turns. After those end, everything is going back to normal, and only those who've left that particular chamber stay in the Primordial Dream. That people can theoretically easily follow is a plot point and mentioned several times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 04-21-2018, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:49:13-07:00","id":1209743,"title":"","content":"This is all explained in the book, though I understand that it can be hard to fully comprehend what you read in your second language.<br /> <br /> Also, to deter you from making new threads left and right, I'm going to say that if you want your questions answered, you need to post your question in the correct thread. I can't control what other people do, but I'm going to keep my mouth shut until you post this in the Ask a Simple Question thread for Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-21-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:51:53-07:00","id":1209744,"title":"","content":"Gonna have to join Master on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:07:43-07:00","id":1209919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1209743#post1209743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all explained in the book, though I understand that it can be hard to fully comprehend what you read in your second language.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so you understand why I spring topic about series of related questions. I found Beast 'corebook language' to be very flowery and some nuances of it are missing my understanding of English. You do not want to here answer - fine. But I find 40 pages long topic not any helpful in finding those nuances related to the corebooks general concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:11:09-07:00","id":1209920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1209738#post1209738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Beast opens a Primordial Pathway, the current physical location and the Chamber's Primordial counterpart overlap - the Primordial Chamber becomes the current physical location for a certain amount of turns. After those end, everything is going back to normal, and only those who've left that particular chamber stay in the Primordial Dream. That people can theoretically easily follow is a plot point and mentioned several times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, number of turns overlapping between material and Dream is in the <b>Beast Players Guide</b>? Those <i>Dreamquake</i> effects? Cause on reading them I understood it's more number of turns that particular Chamber is able to crash those inside it, not that this effect of Chamber could kill people in physical location.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:31:54-07:00","id":1209926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1209919#post1209919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I find 40 pages long topic not any helpful in finding those nuances related to the corebooks general concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, nobody is telling you &quot;read the Ask A Simple Question thread to find your answers.&quot; People are telling you that <i>if you have a simple question, the place to ask it is in the Ask A Simple Question Thread, which exists specifically so that the board does not become cluttered with people making multiple threads asking simple questions.</i>\u200b A certain amount of repetition is accepted as inevitable for those threads precisely because they are so large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1209920#post1209920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, number of turns overlapping between material and Dream is in the <b>Beast Players Guide</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the section on Primordial Paths in the core rulebook. Page 97.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T01:12:53-07:00","id":1209942,"title":"","content":"Okay, so page 97 and 98 of <b>BtP</b> corebook solves most of my questions. We will see if something more comes to my mind on subject, later on.<br /> <br /> <b>Opening Pathways ( also to the Lair )</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, p. 97</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Resolve<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Willpower<br /> (...)<br /> <b>Success: </b>The Pathway successfully opens and lasts for the opening <b>character\u2019s Resolve in turn</b>s.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The Pathway successfully opens and <b>lasts for the rest of the scene</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Other beings in area of open Primordial Pathways</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, p. 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone in the external location attempting to leave while the Pathway is active instead finds themselves transitioning to another Chamber through one of the Lair\u2019s Burrows. Anyone still in the Chamber when the Pathway closes ends up in the external location. Collapsing a Chamber immediately closes any Primordial Pathways open to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:31:14-07:00","id":1210036,"title":"","content":"Wyrd. I'm not sure we're supposed to post exerpts with actual mechanics. It might be copyright infringement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:46:34-07:00","id":1211040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1210036#post1210036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd. I'm not sure we're supposed to post exerpts with actual mechanics. It might be copyright infringement</div> </div> </div> </div>Game mechanics are not something that can be copyrighted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:57:33-07:00","id":1211049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to?p=1211040#post1211040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=